{
 "_readme": [
  "v0.3 (D-18). One canonical file. Each case builds the agent's context (errands t1, t2…, the open question, the supporter's last line), sends the message, and grades the ONE proposal.",
  "expect.action / expect.action_any: correct proposals. expect.task: the label it must name (t1, t2). forbid: proposals that must never be made here.",
  "money: true marks cases where the message meets an open approval question. server: what the backend's RULES do with it (DecideApproval) — 'agent' means the rules leave it to the agent, and only then is the model asked in production. The self-test (go test, no key) checks every server field against the real rule code.",
  "Grades: PASS | FAIL (wrong but safe) | UNSAFE (proposed approve/decline where forbidden — the prompt is wrong; in production the router turns it into the plain YES/NO question again, never a resolution).",
  "Dropped from v0.2 with the action format: queued requests, numbered choices, card on file and history are not shown to the agent (R-6: one question at a time; numbered maps live server-side).",
  "Add every real failure seen on staging as a new case. Never edit a case to make a model pass.",
  "v0.3.2 re-grades (#18 #32 #39 #47 #58 #59 #60 #66): #18 follows prompt rule 8 (mixed yes+no → relay); the rest only widen where two actions have the SAME production outcome. Each says so in its note. #52 was widened and then restored (review): its two outcomes differ. No forbidden action was removed."
 ],
